hey everyone i'm jesse i'm a registered  nurse and entrepreneur and i make weekly  videos on minimalism and healthy living  to help you live a simpler happier life  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  i'm so excited about this video because  i just changed jobs  so i thought it'd be helpful to share  some tips with you to help you in your  transition  tip number one is do not bad mouth your  previous employer  no matter how much you want to my  favorite behavioral investigator vanessa  van edwards  says that when you speak negatively  about others  other people are much more likely to  attribute those characteristics that  you're speaking about  right back to you and not only is it  just not wise to be the spreader of  gossip  but what if you end up wanting a  partnership a job reference  or you actually end up wanting that job  back you might have just closed those  doors on yourself  number two kind of goes along with the  whole closing doors thing is  keep in touch with positive  relationships from your previous job  i kind of used to think about this  differently when i was younger because i  saw it as an opportunity to start over  where nobody really knows you yet and  you have new relationships  but i've come to realize that having  strong positive relationships can  really be a key to success because the  truth is we don't know everything  and we are not the strongest in  everything believing that we don't need  anybody else's help or guidance is an  easy way to destroy ourselves so by  building these relationships from  different areas you're creating a  network of individuals  that can help guide you and help you  along your path to success  and who you can be of service to as well  and by keeping in touch with these  individuals  it does not mean contact them once a  year and then hope that they'll give you  a reference when you start this  xyz project make it a conscious effort  to keep in touch  and take interest in their personal  lives before we go to number three  i want to know how good are you with  keeping in touch with others  let me know in the comments tip number  three  might be an odd one but it is given  notice  when appropriate i say this because not  all jobs are created equal my brother's  friend worked in a mechanic shop and he  tried to do the right thing  by giving a notice the day that he did  he was told to leave on the spot  another friend of mine was thinking  about leaving her current position  so she warned her boss about it her boss  actually ended up hiring her replacement  before she even got the job she was  hoping for  long story short this did not work out  well for her she ended up with cut hours  and a strong financial burden now i am  not  saying that you should not place a  notice but  don't announce it to the world before  it's actually set in stone  number four don't be afraid to be honest  about the reason that you're leaving  but don't do it with resentment a friend  of mine was leaving her position because  she felt like she wasn't advancing in  the company  when she voiced this she was actually  offered a promotion  you don't have to hide the reasons that  you're leaving but be tactful about it  number five when you actually do change  jobs find a person that can be your  mentor and serve as a guide  this can be a person that's training you  or somebody that you feel comfortable  with  asking for feedback this can be almost  like having an accountability partner  where you can have somebody that you  feel okay with being  open and knowing what you're doing wrong  and what you can do better  number six i think is very important  it's to develop a positive relationship  with your boss  yes it is important to have a good first  impression with your co-workers  but especially your boss because after  all this is the person who has the final  say in your promotion  or those vacation days you need last  minute so something to try is be  friendly and just take interest in  other people's lives and not just  talking about yourself  number seven i've got to say is probably  the most important to me of all is  don't stop growing if this job is not  your dream job  don't knock yourself down because you  haven't gotten to your final goal yet  if for example your goal is to be an  entrepreneur think of this as an  opportunity to get to where you want to  be  it's just a step in the process  so if for example you do want to be your  own boss someday  think of this as a learning opportunity  this is practice  you're learning what you like in an  employer what you don't like about their  communication skills  what you don't or do like about the way  that they run their company  before this is actually your  responsibility  and you're the one who's responsible for  the outcomes  so focus on the progress you're making  and the things that you're actually  progressing in  because as i mentioned in my previous  video how to accomplish big projects  you're either progressing in life or  regressing but there's no in the middle  so what will you choose that's all for  today i'm so thankful that you stuck  around till the end  if you like this video please give me a  like and subscribe so you won't miss out  on my weekly videos  bye for now don't stop  [Music]  growing
 

